text @[Tomoya]
text Guess I'll go to the library.
text I begin walking while mumbling to myself.
text I head to the library for no particular reason, just to check it out.
text I climb the stairs, passing students on the way to their club rooms with my long stride.
text When I reach the library door, I can tell that something about it feels different from the way it is during classes.
text In fact, I think this is the first time I've ever seen the sign at the entrance read "Open."
text I look inside through a crack in the sliding door.
text The library is full of activity.
text Still, it's mostly students studying on their own. I can hear the sound of mechanical pencils scribbling away.
text (Most of them probably don't see the library as a place to read books.)
text I conveniently ignore my own shortcomings as I think this.
